 so happened to have  god chilling out in his containment cell  in site-17 perhaps through enlisting the  help of earth's divine arbiter he could  bring an end to the scourge of scp-682  and rocket himself to success in the  process however while dr samet may have  been arrogant he wasn't completely  delusional he knew he didn't have the  standing to address scp-343 directly  much less to ask him for a hand in  destroying scp-682  he'd need a go-between someone with  tenure someone who commanded respect  among scp foundation staff as well as  the very anomalies they governed perhaps  someone who was a little bit anomalous  themselves and who better fits this  description than the living legend dr  jack bright dr samut had of course read  the doctor's personnel files everybody  at the foundation knew about dr bright's  exploits from what he's done to the  various things he isn't allowed to do  which we'll cover in a future video he's  also dug up the scp-963 files the  anomalous medallion keeping dr bright  alive whether he likes it or not while a  discussion of the exact nature of the  medallion isn't something you'd want to  have in front of dr bright himself after  all it is a touchy subject you could  make the argument that the medallion is  the real hymn it is where his soul is  condemned to spend perhaps the rest of  eternity killing and stealing the body  of anyone or anything that touched it  he'd become an immortal parasite  destined to take the finite lives of  others while his own marches on forever  remind you of anyone dr samet got into  contact with dr bright and explained his  plan with bright's help he'd recruit  scp-343  and bring the very wrath of god down  onto the hard-to-destroy reptile of  course while dr samut naturally assumed  himself to be the smartest person in the  room dr bright had a more realistic  assessment of the ambitious young turks  skills he saw sammit for what he truly  was a climber a butt kisser a greedy  power-hungry bureaucrat wearing a lab  coat and he thought that made him a  researcher  it was laughable what dr wright found  less funny though was dr samut's  insistence on calling him scp-963  there's a lot to know about dr bright  but one thing you should definitely  commit to memory is that you should  never under any circumstances call dr  bright scp-963  and if you were forever entwined with a  necklace that doomed you to watch  everyone you know and love age and die  while depriving you of that same release  you'd probably resent being associated  with it too dr bright did agree to  participate in dr samet's hair brain  termination scheme but with a warning  that he did not give lightly if ever dr  samut called him 963 again he would have  one of his own loyal team members  nicknamed the lucky bunch for their high  survival rate compared to other  foundation research teams shoot him in  the foot dr bright steeled himself and  entered 343's containment cell where the  playful deity had taken the form of the  late comedian george burns complete with  his trademark glasses and half-smoked  stogie they made small talk with 343  delivering his usual high-handed cryptic  parables about his plans for dr bright  and everybody else he even momentarily  teased the idea of freeing him from his  curse but dr bright knew better than to  buy into these fairy tales he talked  scp-343 into a cross test but didn't  tell him it was with 682 or that he was  expected to terminate it that was better  left as a surprise dr samut and dr  bright stood in the observation area  outside the cross testing chamber sammit  was giddy with excitement and confidence  in this new experiment dr bright's  reactions were a hell of a lot more  measured he'd been working at the  foundation long enough now to know that  terminating scp-682 was a fool's errand  the only researchers still intent on  trying it we're doing so out of  stubbornness and ego and when 343 and  682 were released into the chamber dr  bride's healthy pessimism was more than  justified 682 attacked a nearby door  attempting to breach containment while  343 looked around confused and seemingly  unable to see anything when he was  ordered to kill 682 he was shocked to  learn 682 was even in the room he  stormed off moments later in a huff  saying he's not one of mine deal with  him yourself  dr bright was unsurprised dr samet was  shocked and furious how could this have  failed they literally had god on their  side this setback would seriously  compromise his chances of rising through  the ranks unless he found a quick way to  make the best out of a bad situation and  save face without even thinking he  turned to dr bright and said fine it  didn't work doesn't matter get yourself  ready 963 you're going in so it was  decided dr bright himself would face off  with scp-682  in  scp-343's place dr bright was a betting  man he loved a good game of chance and  he estimated that his odds of succeeding  were exceptionally low but what would be  the point in refusing even if he  couldn't kill  scp-682 perhaps he would get lucky and  the reptile would kill him instead so  many enticing possibilities dr bright  left to prepare for the coming battle  and because nobody would say that dr  bright wasn't a man of his word he had  one of his assistants shoot dr samut in  the foot a few days later dr bright dr  samut now in a wheelchair while he  recovered from his unfortunate foot  injury and a collection of other  researchers including dr sophia light  were convened in a conference room  planning out their assault on  scp-682 a mechanical staff of sorts was  laying on the table in front of him a  kind of powerful taser capable of firing  out painful bolts of electricity it  would be the only object dr bright  carried into the chamber with him that  day but only as a way of getting 682's  attention not as a weapon the true  weapon was scp-963  the plan was simple  scp-682 would eat dr bright and the  power of  scp-963 would 